= Belief revision — Simple =

'''Belief revision''' studies how a set of beliefs should change when new information arrives.

If the new information fits what you already believe, you may simply add it.

If it conflicts with something you already believe, you may need to remove or change other beliefs to keep the set consistent.

Formal theories ask how to make that change while throwing away as little useful information as possible.

The most famous framework is called AGM belief revision.

Belief revision is not the same as Bayesian inference.

AGM-style systems usually work with beliefs treated as accepted or not accepted, while Bayesian systems often use degrees of belief.

